{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_1769772139#10_1995988892","relevance":2,"reason":"The passage gives direct supporting evidence for an effect on India, a leading non-aligned country: Clinton-Yeltsin diplomacy produced an agreement to halt the sale of Russian rocket parts to India. However, the document is focused on Russia–United States relations, not on non-aligned countries as such.","learned":"Another concrete Yeltsin-era effect on a non-aligned country was Russia curbing rocket/space technology sales to India under U.S. pressure."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ yeltsin india (+ rocket cryogenic) (+ halted sale pressure))","reason":"Search for focused evidence on the Yeltsin-era halt or restriction of Russian rocket/cryogenic technology sales to India, a direct effect on a leading non-aligned country."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ yeltsin india (+ rocket cryogenic) (+ halted sale pressure))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_1769772139#9_1995985252","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q915","rank":2,"snippet":"formed by 12 of the 15 former Soviet constituent republics, leaving out the three Baltic states. The Russian Soviet Federative Socialist Republic became Russia. It was now an independent state that inherited the USSR's UN Security Council permanent membership and became the successor state to the USSR. Strobe Talbott, who was Washington's chief expert on Russia, has argued that Clinton hit it off with Russian Boris Yeltsin, the president of Russia 1991-1999: The personal diplomacy between Clinton and Yeltsin, augmented by the channel that Gore developed with <cover>Yeltsin’s longest-serving prime minister, Victor Chernomyrdin, yielded half a dozen major understandings that either resolved or alleviated disputes over Russia’s role in the post–cold war world. The two presidents were the negotiators in chief of agreements to halt the sale of Russian rocket parts to India; </cover>remove Soviet-era nuclear missiles from Ukraine in exchange for Russian assurances of Ukraine’s sovereignty and security;\" , \"start_char\": 7564.000000 , \"title\": \"Russia–United States relations - Wikipedia\" , \"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russia%E2%80%93United_States_relations\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_1769772139#10_1995988892","rank":1,"relevance":2}]}}
