{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_621764772#0_697667876","relevance":2,"reason":"The document is dedicated to the Non-Aligned Movement and explains that it was created so countries could avoid Cold War bloc polarization, which supports why the Soviet/Yeltsin-era end of the Cold War mattered. However, this segment does not itself state the post-Cold-War effect on non-aligned countries.","learned":"NAM's original purpose was avoiding alignment in the polarized Cold War; this supports the broader answer that the movement's purpose changed after the Cold War ended."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"non-aligned movement\" \"cold war ended\" (+ relevance purpose identity))","reason":"Search for direct passages stating how the end of the Cold War changed the relevance, purpose, or identity of NAM/non-aligned countries, likely yielding more grade-3 evidence."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"non-aligned movement\" \"cold war ended\" (+ relevance purpose identity))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_11_1400344588#1_2953757362","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q922","rank":3,"snippet":", \"segment\": \"Visit Yahoo Home Promoted Josh Rocks Josh Rocks asked in Arts & Humanities History · 1 decade ago how did the cold war affect cuba? 4 Answers<cover>Relevance woody Lv 6 1 decade ago Favorite Answer Economically and diplomatically they only had other communist nations to deal with, which really limited their options. tuffy Lv 7 1 decade ago During the Cold War Cuba had Russia as their main trading partner. When the Cold War ended Cuba's economy took a hit. poornakumar b Lv 7 1 decade ago The whole world between 1945 to 1992 was in the shadow of Cold War. There were innumerable wars and none escaped its shadow. Even a domestic (civil) war had its contestants split into Communist and Capitalist factions and fought on. They were aided and abetted by the first (Capitalist or so-called 'free World') world & the second (Communist) world. The third world some of whom organised into some kind of a neutral 'Non-aligned' movement </cover>was not of any help, being a conglomerate of weak and poor countries. Cuba is Communist (Fidel Castro took over after the Batista dictatorship) and eighty miles across the sea from USA.","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_621764772#9_697691827","rank":1,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_621764772#10_697694105","rank":2,"relevance":3}]}}
