{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_49_1450945554#10_3003043202","relevance":3,"reason":"The document is dedicated to non-alignment/NAM and directly explains a post-Cold-War/Soviet-disintegration effect: the disintegration of alliance systems vindicated the non-aligned position, and afterward NAM increasingly concentrated on economic issues and emancipation. This directly supports how non-aligned countries/their movement were affected by the Yeltsin-era collapse of Soviet power.","learned":"Another direct answer is that after the disintegration of Cold War alliance systems, NAM shifted focus toward economic issues and emancipation rather than military-bloc nonalignment."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"after disintegration\" \"nonaligned movement\" \"economic issues\")","reason":"Search the distinctive direct-answer phrase to find additional dedicated documents or passages explaining NAM's post-Soviet shift toward economic issues."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"after disintegration\" \"nonaligned movement\" \"economic issues\")"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_49_1450945554#9_3003039740","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q926","rank":1,"snippet":"struggles that rend the world. We will not hitch our carriage to any nation’s engine and be drawn along their railway line. 2 The criteria of non-alignment determined as early as June 1961 at Cairo were: A country should follow an independent policy based on peaceful coexistence and non-alignment or show a trend in favor of such a policy. It should consistently have supported movements for national independence. It should not be a member of multilateral military alliances concluded in the context of Great Power conflicts. If it has conceded military bases, these concessions should not have been made in the context of Great Power conflicts. If it is a member of a bilateral or regional defense arrangement, this should not be in the context of Great Power conflicts. The disintegration of alliance systems in recent years is indeed a vindication of the non-aligned position. <cover>After disintegration, the nonaligned movement (NAM) is increasingly concentrating on economic issues </cover>and emancipation.\" , \"start_char\": 5830.000000 , \"title\": \"Non-alignment Movement - Political Science\" , \"url\": \"https://www.politicalscienceview.com/non-alignment/\" }"}}
