{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"non-aligned movement\" \"end of bipolarism\")"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_49_1450945554#7_3003032844","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q945","rank":1,"snippet":"of non-alignment and their impact on international relations are summarized as below: 1. World Peace: 2. End of Cold War: 3. <cover>End of Bipolarism: 4. End of Colonialism: 5. End of Racialism: 6. End of Military Alliances: 7. Minimized the arms race: 8. Preservation of Independence: 9. Strengthened U.N.O: 10. Universal International System: 11. More Economic Aid: 12. New Economic Order: 13. New Communication Order: Criticism: 1. Ambiguous Concept: 2. Not a Model of Behavior: 3. Selfish Policy: 4. Opportunistic and Immoral: 5. Bloc Mentality: 6. Harsh towards West: 7. Disunity: 8. Serious Dilemma: 9 Hypocrisy: 10. Labour Union Approach: 11 . Factionalism: 12. Like Alliance System: 13. Worthless Declarations and Conferences: 14. No Results: The relevance of Non-Alignment: Irrelevant and Invalid : Still Relevant and Valid: REFERENCES: Share this: \" , \"segment\": \"As a positive concept, it has several dimensions; naturally, non-alignment should oppose certain values and at the same time promote some others which are in harmony with its basic orientation. The chief goals of the non-aligned movement </cover>in the fifties and sixties re decolonize and preserve international peace. Of late, it has been contributing positively to attaining a new "}}
